<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S6.T1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results for CoT length prediction. Values are in rMAE, hence the lower the better. The best results are highlighted. Baseline methods are introduced in Section <a href="#S6.SS1" title="6.1 Experimental Setup and Benchmarks ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Fuel Gauge: Estimating Chain-of-Thought Length Ahead of Time in Large Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>. GPQA-Diamond and MathVison show the generalizability of Fuel Gauge from general tasks to specialized tasks, and LongVideoBench shows the both the cross-task and cross-modality (<span id="S6.T1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, text-image to text-video) generalizability.</span></figcaption>
