<td id="A4.T7.3.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">82.24k</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table S7</span>: </span><span id="A4.T7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Overhead of Fuel Gauge on NVIDIA A6000 GPU. Results show that the time and memory spent in Fuel Gauge is negligible.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Figures for CoT Length Modulations in Section <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Fuel Gauge: Estimating Chain-of-Thought Length Ahead of Time in Large Multimodal Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> are in Next Page.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
